# Publish or verify local

After finishing meaningful product/code changes in this repo:

1. **Prefer publish:** commit (when the user asked or when continuing an agreed ship), push to `main`, confirm CI is green, and briefly confirm production (`https://www.arabyaai.com`) responds for the touched surface when practical.
2. **If not publishing yet:** start or reuse `npm run dev`, then verify the changed routes/APIs on localhost (at least HTTP 200 / no crash) before ending the turn.
3. Do not leave the user with “fixed locally, unshipped” unless they explicitly asked to skip deploy.
4. Tell the user which of the two was done (pushed commit SHA + CI, or local URL/port checked).
